  "notes": "Modified cash basis. Governmental receipts/disbursements from the governmental funds statement (p6, Totals column); transfers in 106,475 (General) and out 119,529 (ARPA) printed on p6 (net 13,054 out); roll-forward 2,942,853 + 2,183,575 - 2,348,582 + 106,475 - 119,529 = 2,764,792. Beginning/ending balance = governmental fund balances (p7; also p4 total assets 2,764,792 / 2024 totals 2,942,853). Business-type lines from the proprietary statement of revenues, expenses and changes in net position (p10) with measure net position: 6,760,693 + 3,277,280 - 3,100,670 + transfers 13,054 = 6,950,357. Business-type receipts total is computed (charges 3,273,207 + interest 2,123 + sale of property 1,950). The proprietary cash flow statement (p11-12) has blank cash beginning/ending lines so proprietary is null. Balance sheet is the government-wide Statement of Net Position, Total column (p1). Detail: the General Fund by-department schedule (p15-16) is recorded by department column; the all-fund-types budget schedule (p13-14, one combined General All-Purpose Fund column incl. proprietary) is not recorded to avoid double counting and cannot be split by fund. Detail Fire/Police/Pool/Park/Library/Summer Youth columns are intra-General-Fund departments; their operating transfers (p16) are internal to the General Fund and net to the fund's 106,475. Interest line on p6 columns: Keno 396, CDBG 554, ARPA 1,199 (Street's 8,025 and CDBG 17,706 belong to the Other row). Read pages 1-16 of 16"
}